texts[105]="Announcements can have an optional condition tree using the Switch condition picker, including All, Any and Not. The tree runs only after a matching spell/event and duplicate check. Only a match permits the announcement's message and sound. Unavailable observations remain unavailable under Not. Announcements without a condition keep their existing behavior.\010"
texts[106]="Help is a compact formatted native article with the same chrome, Help at the top right, X/Escape/right-click closure, and no report-copy or extra Close controls. Main-window Help includes the authored field documentation. General fields follow the same order as the page, without separate question marks beside controls. The authored text is shared data used by both renderers. Rotation/cooldown/branch Help describes clickable elements and drag/edit behavior. A condition card\226\128\153s summary Help explains its interactions; with fields open, Help appends that condition\226\128\153s specific help beneath those fields. Diagnostic and full-expression copy dialogs remain separate.\010"
texts[107]="    assert(pane.children[1].type=='RM-ConditionSlider' and pane.children[2].text=='Number help','help replaced the editable field')\010"
texts[108]="test('expanded condition help appends below live fields instead of replacing them',function()\010"
texts[109]="test('explicit summary navigation exits Help while Help toggle alone restores its prior view',function()\010"
texts[110]="    card.controls.help:Click();assert(shell.canvas.cards[1].model.ownHeight==before)\010"
texts[111]="    assert(card.fields:GetHeight()>=card.helpText:GetStringHeight()+16)\010"
texts[112]="test('group Help measures its text after compact native controls and clears that height on close',function()\010"
texts[113]="test('group Help opens inline without creating a recursive group editor',function()\010"
